        "name": "USN-5807-3",
        "description": "USN-5807-1 fixed a vulnerability in libXpm. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 14.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   Marco Ivaldi discovered that libXpm incorrectly handled certain XPM files.  If a user or automated system were tricked into opening a specially crafted  XPM file, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause libXpm  to stop responding, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2022-46285)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2022-46285"
        ]
      },
